00:20:52.334 --> 00:20:58.400
Here’s one example where I’m using OpenAI Dot.

251
00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:05.946
I’m asking it to update me. It says it
failed. Then I ask, “Why did it fail?”

252
00:21:05.976 --> 00:21:08.350
If it knows why it failed, it can

253
00:21:10.736 --> 00:21:13.626
actually, uh, correct it and make it work.

254
00:21:13.838 --> 00:21:15.752
One thing is important.

255
00:21:16.218 --> 00:21:19.332
At the beginning, you need to teach the AI,

256
00:21:20.278 --> 00:21:22.928
for example, how to connect to the HPC and

257
00:21:22.958 --> 00:21:25.832
how many processors or how much RAM to use.

258
00:21:26.458 --> 00:21:32.404
I ask it to study HPC job submission,

259
00:21:34.238 --> 00:21:39.762
how submission works, then train the skill

260
00:21:42.328 --> 00:21:45.502
so you can reuse it to help

261
00:21:46.228 --> 00:21:48.202
run successful simulations.

262
00:21:48.598 --> 00:21:50.842
Here’s an example of AI

263
00:21:51.498 --> 00:21:56.114
