297
00:24:40.026 --> 00:24:43.220
My voice will stay on my local desktop.

298
00:24:45.286 --> 00:24:49.680
We show in detail how AI agents work

299
00:24:51.166 --> 00:24:52.840
and what problems they can solve.

300
00:24:53.188 --> 00:24:55.490
“Should I use OpenCode or Codex?”

301
00:24:55.916 --> 00:25:01.130
OpenCode can connect
to whatever LLM API you want.

302
00:25:02.546 --> 00:25:04.140
Codex is for ChatGPT.

303
00:25:06.776 --> 00:25:08.050
There’s a difference,

304
00:25:09.556 --> 00:25:11.070
because you can choose whatever you want.

305
00:25:13.830 --> 00:25:16.944
[Audience] Just a few
words, if you don’t mind.

306
00:25:17.430 --> 00:25:20.310
Is this applicable for [unclear], for example,

307
00:25:20.340 --> 00:25:25.086
for a molecule, especially that you
