308
00:25:25.540 --> 00:25:30.534
And, for example, you go with two
parts, and then you said…

309
00:25:30.860 --> 00:25:32.996
[Presenter] Of course, it is applicable.

310
00:25:33.740 --> 00:25:36.626
You want to run a simulation with ORCA.

311
00:25:37.080 --> 00:25:41.898
You can ask the LLM to connect with

312
00:25:41.928 --> 00:25:46.854
ORCA to do a simulation, again, TD-DFT.

313
00:25:47.630 --> 00:25:48.798
It’s all there.

314
00:25:49.624 --> 00:25:56.732
For synthesis, the AI has to be able
to access a synthesis database and find

315
00:25:56.762 --> 00:25:58.018
the best way of synthesis.

316
00:25:58.586 --> 00:26:02.140
Whatever the computer can do,

317
00:26:03.636 --> 00:26:07.980
just allow the AI to use the tool
that can do this faster for you.

318
00:26:10.454 --> 00:26:13.008
It’s also important to formulate a question.

319
00:26:13.932 --> 00:26:15.408
The right direction is important.

320
00:26:16.044 --> 00:26:20.638
And find a simulation that
agrees with experiment.

321
00:26:20.824 --> 00:26:26.228
What constraints do you need
to put in as the AI simulates?

322
00:26:26.812 --> 00:26:32.088
Being able to audit the evidence
of your simulation becomes important,

323
00:26:32.342 --> 00:26:33.978
rather than running a simulation.

324
00:26:35.938 --> 00:26:37.170
Computing becomes easy,

325
00:26:38.216 --> 00:26:41.330
but defining a good problem
and proving the result will matter.

326
00:26:41.476 --> 00:26:43.500
A proven result connects
back to the real world.

